{
  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only multiprofile+avgpool (config_002, acc=0.591) is the clear best so far, while image-only ResNet50 (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak. The critical open question is whether the image modality provides complementary information when fused with the strong RNA signal, or whether it merely adds noise. config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the minimal extension of config_002: it holds RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical and introduces only the image branch and concat fusion. This isolates the effect of adding the image modality. If it fails to beat 0.591, we learn that ResNet50 image features are not complementary and can redirect budget toward better RNA encoders or a stronger image encoder (ViT-L). If it does help, it confirms the multimodal direction and justifies further fusion-architecture exploration. Under a tight budget, resolving whether multimodal is worthwhile at all is the highest-value single experiment."
}

